\n\
If I block with the 1/3, the Fortune Teller survives (3 damage to a 1/3... wait, 3 damage to a 3-toughness creature means it survives). The Voyager is 3/3, my Fortune Teller is 1/3. Blocking: Fortune Teller takes 3 damage, has 3 toughness, survives. Voyager takes 1 damage, survives. So I can block safely and take no damage.\n\
\n\
Wait, but should I block? Blocking with the 1/3 is safe — it survives and I prevent 3 damage. That seems good. There's no downside really, unless the opponent has a trick. The opponent has 4 cards in hand and all lands tapped (Kyoshi Village, North Pole Gates, Plains all tapped). So no mana for tricks. Blocking is safe and free.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, let me check: Kyoshi Village (tapped), North Pole Gates (tapped), Plains (tapped). All three lands tapped. They played Earth King's Lieutenant this turn presumably (it's sick). So they have no mana available. No tricks possible. Block with Fortune Teller — it survives, I take 0 damage.\n\
