My board: Clue Token, Foggy Swamp Spirit Keeper 2/4 (lifelink), Tiger-Seal 3/3 (vigilance, taps at upkeep — the trigger is on the stack now), 3 Islands + 1 Swamp.\n\
\n\
Opponent's board: Airbender Ascension (4 quest counters — will trigger at their end step), 3 Ally tokens 1/1 (two sick), Earth King's Lieutenant 7/7 trample, 2 Invasion Reinforcements 1/1 (sick), South Pole Voyager 3/3. Lands: Kyoshi Village, North Pole Gates, 3 Plains (one untapped).\n\
\n\
That's a scary board. Earth King's Lieutenant is 7/7 trample. My Spirit Keeper is 2/4 — blocks it but 3 trample damage gets through. Tiger-Seal 3/3 blocks but 4 trample through.\n\
\n\
The upkeep trigger will tap Tiger-Seal. I can respond... but the trigger just taps it. Tiger-Seal untaps when I draw my second card each turn. I have a Clue token — I could crack it to draw. If I draw for turn + crack clue = 2 cards drawn, Tiger-Seal untaps and Spirit Keeper makes a 1/1 Spirit token.\n\
\n\
Wait, order: my draw step happens after upkeep. So I'll draw my card for turn (1st card), then I can crack the Clue (2nd card drawn) → Tiger-Seal untaps, Spirit Keeper creates a 1/1 Spirit.\n\
\n\
Right now, the upkeep trigger is on the stack. I could crack the Clue now, but that would only be my first card drawn this turn — no triggers. Actually, cards drawn this turn: 0. If I crack clue now, that's 1 card. Then draw step = 2nd card → triggers. Either way works. Better to wait and see what I draw first? Actually cracking now vs after draw — same number of cards. Let me just pass and let the trigger resolve, then draw, then decide.\n\
\n\
Actually, there's a subtle point: if I crack the Clue now (in upkeep), I draw 1 card. Then in draw step I draw — that's my 2nd card → Tiger-Seal untaps and Spirit Keeper triggers. That's fine.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, let the tap trigger resolve, draw step draw (1st card), then crack clue (2nd card) → untap Tiger-Seal + Spirit token. Same result but I get to see my draw first before deciding to crack. That's slightly better for information.\n\
\n\
But there's a consideration: Zuko's Conviction — I can cast it to return Forecasting Fortune Teller to hand, or kicked (4+B = 5 mana) to put it onto the battlefield tapped. I have 4 mana now. Kicked costs 5. Not yet.\n\
\n\
My hand: Island, Island, North Pole Patrol, Zuko's Conviction.\n\
\n\
Opponent's threat: Earth King's Lieutenant 7/7 trample is huge. Next turn they attack with the team. My blockers: Spirit Keeper 2/4, Tiger-Seal 3/3 (if untapped), plus potentially a 1/1 Spirit token, plus Fortune Teller 1/3 if I recast it, plus North Pole Patrol 2/3.\n\
\n\
North Pole Patrol is great here — waterbend {3}, tap: tap target creature an opponent controls. That can tap down the Lieutenant every turn! That's key. North Pole Patrol costs {2}{U} = 3 mana. I have 4 mana. Playing it this turn gives me a tapper for their big threat.\n\
\n\
Also Zuko's Conviction to get back Fortune Teller for another blocker + clue.\n\
\n\
Plan: Let upkeep trigger resolve (Tiger-Seal taps). Draw for turn. Then decide. Play North Pole Patrol this turn (3 mana), keep B up? Or play Island, cast Patrol, keep mana.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — I should think about North Pole Patrol's waterbend ability: {3}, {T}: tap target creature. That's 3 mana + tap. So each turn I can spend 3 mana to tap down the Lieutenant. That's expensive but it neutralizes the 7/7 trample.\n\
\n\
Also the {T}: untap another target permanent — I could use it to untap Tiger-Seal after it taps itself! North Pole Patrol taps to untap Tiger-Seal. But summoning sickness — Patrol can't tap the turn it enters.\n\
\n\
Let me think about the bigger picture. Opponent is at 28 life gaining life from Voyager triggers. They have a huge board. I'm at 14. This is looking rough. I need to stabilize.\n\
\n\
Key plays this turn:\n\
1. Draw for turn.\n\
2. Crack Clue → 2nd card drawn → Tiger-Seal untaps, get a 1/1 Spirit token, draw a card.\n\
3. Play an Island (5 mana).\n\
4. Cast North Pole Patrol (3 mana) — leaves 2 mana.\n\
5. Maybe cast Zuko's Conviction for {B} to return Fortune Teller? Leaves 1 mana, can't cast Fortune Teller this turn (costs... let me check — Forecasting Fortune Teller, probably {1}{U}? It's a 1/3 that makes a clue. Probably 2 mana).\n\
\n\
Actually, let me first see what I draw. The immediate decision: respond to the upkeep trigger. I'll just pass — let it resolve. Actually, should I crack the clue in response? No benefit. Pass.\n\
\n\
Letme pass priority now.",
