Should I attack? Opponent has a 7/7 trampler and 3/3 plus several 1/1s. If I attack with Tiger-Seal (3/3) and Spirit Keeper (2/4), they can block with 1/1s easily. The 7/7 would block and kill anything. Attacking seems bad — they have huge blockers. My Spirit Keeper has lifelink; attacking into a 7/7 just loses my creature. No point attacking. Better to stay back on defense since opponent has a massive board and I'm at 14.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — opponent's creatures are mostly tapped? Let me check: the board shows their creatures without \"tapped\" notation except lands. Actually last turn summary said \"all tapped\" — but this is a new turn (turn 5 is my turn). Their creatures untapped on their turn... wait, turn 5 is MY turn. Their creatures would have untapped at the start of their turn 4... no wait.\n\
\n\
Let me re-read. Turn 5 COMBAT - PilotA (me). It's my turn 5. Opponent's creatures: Earth King's Lieutenant 7/7, South Pole Voyager 3/3, Ally tokens, Invasion Reinforcements — none shown as tapped. The sick ones were just played (Invasion Reinforcements sick, Ally tokens sick). Wait, but it's my turn — their creatures shouldn't be sick from my turn... Actually \"sick\" means summoning sickness; if they were played on opponent's last turn (turn 4), they'd still be sick on my turn 5? No — summoning sickness wears off at the start of the controller's turn. If they were played on opponent's turn 4, they're sick during my turn 5 and will lose sickness at start of opponent's turn 5.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually the recap says opponent played Airbender Ascension and Invasion Reinforcements... The Airbender Ascension airbends a creature (exiles until... airbend = exile, and owner can cast for {2}?). Anyway.\n\
\n\
Attack decision: Attacking with Tiger-Seal 3/3 and Spirit Keeper 2/4 into their board: they have 7/7, 3/3, and two 1/1s that can block (the non-sick ones: Ally Token 1/1 not sick, Earth King's Lieutenant, South Pole Voyager). They'd block Tiger-Seal with the 7/7 or just chump with 1/1s. Bad attack. I gain nothing. Stay back.\n\
\n\
I'll skip attacking. Then postcombat main: I have Waterbending Lesson ({3}{U} draw 3) but my lands are all tapped except... Board shows: Island x4 tapped, Swamp tapped. All 5 lands tapped. So I can't cast anything this turn. Hand: Island, Island, Waterbending Lesson, Zuko's Conviction.\n\
\n\
So: skip attack, pass to end turn. Next turn I'll have 6 mana (play Island → 6 lands) and can cast Waterbending Lesson drawing 3, which synergizes with Tiger-Seal/Spirit Keeper card-draw triggers.\n\
\n\
Defensive plan for their turn 5: They have 7/7 trample, 3/3, and 1/1s. I have Tiger-Seal 3/3 (untapped via draw trigger), Spirit Keeper 2/4, North Pole Patrol 2/3, Spirit token 1/1 (can't block non-Spirits). North Pole Patrol can tap down a creature — but it has summoning sickness now, will be usable next turn. Waterbend {3} + tap to tap target creature. That could tap the 7/7 on their turn. Good.\n\
\n\
Skip attack.",
