Opponent's turn 8: they untap everything. Lieutenant 13/13 trample + Katara + Voyager + Snowballers + 3 tokens + 2 Reinforcements = 8 attackers, 26 power. I have 4 blockers. Even if I block 4 non-tramplers, Lieutenant tramples for 11+. Dead unless I topdeck an answer from the Clue draw or turn-8 draw.\n\
\n\
Hmm, is there anything better? What about NOT cracking the Clue and instead... no, drawing is the only way to find an answer.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — maybe I should think about what answers could be in the deck. This is the Avatar: The Last Airbender set (TLA). U/B waterbend deck. Possible removal: \"Water Whip\" (maybe a bounce?), \"Yue, the Moon Spirit\"? I genuinely don't know the set well. There might be a card like \"Bend the Elements\"... Let me just play optimally: maximize cards seen and blockers.\n\
\n\
One more idea: instead of Otter-Penguin, cast Teo {3}{U} 1/4 flying — a 1/4 is a sturdier blocker than 2/1 (survives blocking 1/1s and 2/2s). 1/4 flying can block any non-flyer too. With 3 mana remaining after Fortune Teller + Clue crack... wait let me recount.\n\
\n\
Lands after playing Island: 6 Islands + 1 Swamp = 7 mana. Plus Humble Merchant {T}: {C} = 8 total.\n\
\n\
- Fortune Teller {1}{U}: 2 mana (say Swamp + Island). Remaining: 5 Islands + Merchant = 6.\n\
- Clue crack {2}: 2 Islands. Remaining: 3 Islands + Merchant = 4.\n\
- Teo {3}{U}: 3 Islands. Remaining: Merchant (1 colorless).\n\
\n\
That works! Teo 1/4 flying is a much better blocker than Otter-Penguin 2/1. And Teo's attack trigger could loot later. So cast Teo instead of Otter-Penguin.\n\
\n\
Final board for their turn 8: Tiger-Seal 3/3, Fortune Teller 1/3, Teo 1/4, Merchant 1/1, 3 Spirit tokens (useless as blockers vs their board), Spirit Keeper tapped (untaps turn 8 for me... no wait, opponent's turn 8 comes before my turn 8; Spirit Keeper untaps on MY turn 8, so it's tapped during their attack — useless).\n\
\n\
So 4 blockers vs 8 attackers including a 13/13 trampler. Still dead to an alpha strike unless the Clue draw or my turn-8 draw finds an answer (bounce/tap/removal). Actually — is there any chance they don't alpha strike? They're at 34, I'm at 1. They might fear tricks. But with Honest Work already used and my board known, they should just swing. I need the topdeck.\n\
\n\
What answers might exist in my remaining 22 cards? I've seen ~38 cards? No — library 22, I've drawn... opening 7 + turns 2-7 draws (6) + Lesson 3 + Clue cracks... Let me not bother. Just dig and hope.\n\
\n\
Also: should I keep 1 Island untapped for a potential instant? I have no instants in hand. No.\n\
\n\
Also consider: don't crack the Clue this turn; instead hold it? No — the untap of Tiger-Seal this turn matters for blocking, and the extra Spirit token is a waterbend resource... but Patrol is gone (Humble Merchant). Spirit tokens can't block their creatures. So Spirit tokens are only useful as waterbend fodder or... nothing. But the CARD drawn is the point.\n\
\n\
Alright, also should I attack this turn? My creatures: Tiger-Seal will be untapped after Clue crack; Fortune Teller summoning sick (just cast); Teo summoning sick; Otter not cast. Attacking with Tiger-Seal into their board (all tapped now, but they untap)... they'd just block with a 1/1 or take 3. I'm at 1 life — I can't race 34. Keep everything back. Actually, attacking with Tiger-Seal: they have tons of blockers next turn, and I need Tiger-Seal to block. No attack.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually, hmm: should I even cast Fortune Teller this turn? What if I instead hold everything and... no, there's no benefit. Cast everything, maximize board + dig.\n\
\n\
Let me also double check the Clue crack timing: I've drawn 1 card this turn (my draw step). Fortune Teller ETB makes a Clue (no draw). Cracking Clue = draw #2 → triggers both Tiger-Seal (untap) and Spirit Keeper (token), and Otter-Penguin isn't out yet (if I cast Teo, no trigger). Good.\n\
\n\
One question: order of casting Teo vs cracking Clue — doesn't matter for triggers. Crack Clue first to see what I draw before deciding? If the Clue draw is an answer (e.g., a removal spell), I might want mana to cast it! E.g., if I draw a bounce spell costing 2-3, I'd want mana open. So: crack Clue BEFORE casting Teo. If the drawn card is an instant-speed answer, keep mana for it; if not, cast Teo.\n\
\n\
Actually the Clue draw might be a land too. Fine.\n\
\n\
Plan finalized:\n\
1. Kicker: no.\n\
2. Play Island.\n\
3. Cast Fortune Teller.\n\
4. Crack Clue, draw (triggers resolve: Tiger-Seal untaps, Spirit token).\n\
5. Evaluate drawn card; cast Teo if nothing better.\n\
6. Pass.\n\
\n\
Now the immediate decision: \"Pay Kicker {4}?\" → choice=no.\n\
\n\
