Total toughness available turn 8 (optimistic): Tiger-Seal 3 + Fortune Teller 3 + Merchant 1 + Otter 2 = 9. Lieutenant will be at least 13/13, likely 16/16 after Ascension flicker. 13-9=4, 16-9=7. Either way lethal. And opponent will also attack with everything else (Voyager 3/3, Katara 3/3, Snowballers 2/2, tokens 1/1s, Reinforcements 1/1s) — I can't block everything anyway. Spirit tokens can't block non-Spirits. So I have 4 real blockers (Tiger-Seal, Fortune Teller, Merchant, Otter if cast). Opponent has ~8 attackers. Even without trample I die.\n\
\n\
Conclusion: Without drawing an answer, I'm dead on turn 8 no matter what. So the Clue draw is everything. And actually — even if I draw an answer for the Lieutenant, I still face a wide board. E.g., if I bounce/tap the Lieutenant, I still face Voyager+Katara+Snowballers+tokens+Reinforcements = 3+3+2+1+1+1+1 = 12 power attacking. My blockers: Tiger-Seal 3/3, Fortune Teller 1/3, Merchant 1/1, Otter 2/1, Spirit Keeper tapped. I can block 4 creatures. 8 attackers, 4 blocked (kill some), ~4+ unblocked × ~1-3 power... Let me see: block Voyager (3/3) with Tiger-Seal (trade), block Katara with Fortune Teller (Fortune Teller dies, 1/3 vs 3/3), block Snowballers with Otter (2/1 vs 2/2, Otter dies, Snowballers survives... 2/1 deals 2 to 2/2 kills it actually! 2 damage to 2/2 = dead. Snowballers deals 2 to Otter 2/1 = dead. Trade), block a token with Merchant (Merchant 1/1 vs 1/1 trade). Unblocked: Reinforcements x2 (1/1 each) + 3 tokens (1/1) = 5 damage. I'm at 1. Dead anyway.\n\
\n\
Ugh. The board is just too wide. I need a sweeper or multiple answers. My remaining deck — do I have a sweeper? Unknown. 22 cards, 5 in hand, drawn ~15 cards. \n\
\n\
OK let me stop over-planning and just resolve the Clue. The draw determines everything. Let me pass priority.\n\
\n\
Actually — one consideration: should I respond to my own Clue activation with anything? No reason. Pass.\n\
\n\
Also should I chat? It's been a while. The instructions say chat at least once every 2 turn cycles. Let me send a message after resolving. Something like acknowledging the tight spot: \"Down to 1 life — need a miracle off this Clue.\" That's fine.\n\
\n\
Letme pass priority now.",
