        "pool_size": 0,
        "reasoning": "This is booster 1, pick 1 of a draft. Let me evaluate the pack.\n\
\n\
The pack is from an Avatar: The Last Airbender themed set. Cards:\n\
\n\
1. Swamp - basic land, don't take.\n\
2. Deadly Precision {B} - destroy target creature, but additional cost pay {4} or sacrifice artifact/creature. That's a bad removal spell - effectively 5 mana or sacrifice. Weak.\n\
3. Forecasting Fortune Teller {1}{U} - 2 mana creature (presumably 2/1 or similar) that makes a Clue. Decent.\n\
4. Rumble Arena - land, colorless, scry 1 on ETB, can add any color for {1}{T}. Fixing land, common. Decent for mana fixing.\n\
5. Origin of Metalbending {1}{G} - modal: destroy artifact/enchantment or +1/+1 counter and indestructible. Okay combat trick.\n\
6. Kyoshi Battle Fan {2} - equipment that makes a 1/1 white Ally token, gives +1/+0. Decent in Ally deck.\n\
7. Platypus-Bear {1}{G/U} - defender, mills 2, can attack if Lesson in graveyard. Meh.\n\
8. Foggy Bottom Swamp - tapland B/G with cycling-ish draw. Fixing.\n\
9. Dragonfly Swarm {1}{U}{R} - flying, ward 1, power = noncreature nonland cards in graveyard. Multicolor uncommon, spells matter.\n\
10. Energybending {2} - cantrip that gives lands all basic types. Mana fixing cantrip.\n\
11. Zuko, Exiled Prince {3}{R} - Firebending 3, {3}: exile top card, play this turn. Solid red uncommon.\n\
12. Earth Rumble {3}{G} - Earthbend 2 + fight. Decent green uncommon.\n\
13. Wartime Protestors {3}{R} - Rare, haste, Ally tribal payoff. Allies give +1/+1 counter and haste. Rare but build-around.\n\
14. Tiger-Seal {U} - Rare, 1 mana creature with vigilance, taps at upkeep, untaps when you draw second card each turn. Cheap blue rare. Stats unknown but presumably 1/2 or 2/1? Tiger-Seal... In the actual Avatar set, Tiger-Seal is a 1U? No wait, it's {U} - 1 mana. Let me think: \"Tiger-Seal {U} Vigilance. At the beginning of your upkeep, tap this. Whenever you draw your second card each turn, untap this.\" Probably a 2/1 or 1/2. Actually in the real set (TLE?), Tiger-Seal is a 2/1 for U? Hmm.\n\
\n\
First pick: best card overall. Options: Zuko (solid but 4 mana), Wartime Protestors (rare, build-around ally), Tiger-Seal (cheap efficient rare), Dragonfly Swarm (gold card, strong if spells deck).\n\
\n\
In draft, first pick should be a strong, efficient card. Tiger-Seal at {U} is very efficient - a one-mana creature with vigilance that can untap repeatedly with card draw. It keeps you open to blue. Cheap cards are flexible.\n\
\n\
Wartime Protestors is 4 mana 3/3? (probably 3/3 haste). Ally tribal payoff - good if you draft allies, and there are allies in the set (Kyoshi Battle Fan makes an Ally token). But 4-mana rare that needs support.\n\
\n\
Zuko is a solid uncommon, 4 mana 4/3? Firebending 3 is strong. Actually Zuko, Exiled Prince is a 4/3? Let me recall: Zuko, Exiled Prince {3}{R} 4/3? I believe it's a 3/3 with firebending 3. Hmm, actual card: Zuko, Exiled Prince - 3R, 3/3? Firebending 3, \"{3}: Exile the top card of your library. You may play that card this turn.\" I think it's a 4/3. Either way solid.\n\
\n\
