\n\
Hmm, but should I consider playing both Zuko's Convictions? The second one over... maybe North Pole Patrol or Pirate Peddlers? Zuko's is good grindy value. With kicker it's reanimation for 5BB total... kicker {4} so {4}{B} = 5 mana total? Kicker {4} plus {B} = {4}{B}, puts creature onto battlefield tapped. That's good late game.\n\
\n\
Removal count: Deadly Precision (destroy), Sold Out (exile), Crashing Wave (tap + stun). That's light-ish but okay. Lost Days could be added for more removal. Maybe cut Pirate Peddlers or Flexible Waterbender... Flexible Waterbender is already cut.\n\
\n\
Let me think about whether to include Lost Days over something. Lost Days is 5 mana, puts creature second from top or bottom, makes a Clue. It's slow but it's removal + clue. I have only 2 hard removal spells. Crashing Wave is more of a tempo play.\n\
\n\
Alternative: cut Pirate Peddlers (3 mana 2/2 deathtouch?) for Lost Days. Pirate Peddlers has synergy with sacrificing clues/food though. The deck has lots of clues, so Peddlers can grow. I think Peddlers is fine.\n\
\n\
Or cut Zuko's Conviction for Lost Days? Zuko's provides late-game value; Lost Days provides tempo removal. Hmm. The deck is slow/grindy with the draw-two theme, so value is good. But 5-mana removal is bad in a deck that wants to tap out for card advantage... Actually both are 5 mana-ish effects.\n\
\n\
Let me also consider: should Teo make the cut? Yes, Teo is a flier payoff with looting—helps enable draw-two triggers... actually looting draws a card, which counts. Teo + fliers = extra draws each turn, enabling second-card-draw triggers. Great with Messenger Hawks.\n\
\n\
What about Waterbender Ascension? Quest counters on combat damage, draws cards at 4+ counters—more draw-two enablers. Yes, include.\n\
\n\
Hama: {2}{U/B}{U/B}{U/B} — costs 5 mana, can be cast with UB hybrid. Mill + steal a card from graveyard. Solid. Include.\n\
\n\
Mana base for UB: we have Swamp, Island basics unlimited. Drafted lands: Misty Palms Oasis (W/B), North Pole Gates (W/U), Foggy Bottom Swamp (B/G), Rumble Arena (colorless). For UB, the duals that help: Misty Palms (B), North Pole Gates (U), Foggy Bottom (B). They enter tapped. Rumble Arena gives colorless or any color with 1.\n\
\n\
17 lands: probably 8 Island, 6 Swamp, plus North Pole Gates, Misty Palms Oasis, Foggy Bottom Swamp = 17. Or include Rumble Arena too. That's a lands-step decision anyway.\n\
\n\
The double U cards: Crashing Wave {U}{U}, Spirit Water Revival {1}{U}{U}. Double B: Canyon Crawler {4}{B}{B} (cut). So we want enough blue sources — maybe 9 blue sources, 8 black.\n\
\n\
Should I reconsider the white splash? White cards available: Glider Kids x2 (decent 3-mana 2/2 flier scry), Razor Rings (good removal), Airbending Lesson (removal + cantrip), Jeong Jeong's Deserters (2-mana 1/1 with counter). With 3 white sources, splashing 1-2 white cards is plausible. Razor Rings is arguably better than Lost Days/Sold Out? Sold Out is 4 mana exile at sorcery... instant? Unknown, probably sorcery. Razor Rings is 2 mana dealing 4 to attacking/blocking with lifegain—efficient.\n\
\n\
But adding white means a 3-color deck with shaky mana. The dual lands are taplands. I think staying UB is cleaner. The UB pool has enough playables and a coherent theme.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider cutting North Pole Patrol. It's a 3-mana creature (probably 2/3?) with utility tap ability. It also enables... it untaps permanents, can help with waterbend by untapping? Waterbend taps artifacts/creatures to pay costs. North Pole Patrol can untap a permanent, net. It's fine. Keep.\n\
\n\
Otter-Penguin: 2-mana (probably 1/1 or 2/1) that becomes unblockable with second draw. Works with Waterbender Ascension (combat damage triggers) and draws. Keep.\n\
\n\
Tiger-Seal: rare, 1-mana vigilance that taps itself at upkeep, untaps on second draw. Basically a 1-mana creature that can attack every other turn unless you draw two. With the theme, it's a 1-mana attacker every turn. Good with Ascension too. Keep.\n\
\n\
Forecasting Fortune Teller: 2-mana 1/2? with clue. Fine filler, enables clues. Keep.\n\
\n\
Callous Inspector: 1-mana menace, clue on death, pings you. Good aggressive one-drop. Keep.\n\
\n\
So the 23:\n\
\n\
1. Tiger-Seal\n\
2. Callous Inspector\n\
3. Otter-Penguin\n\
4. Knowledge Seeker\n\
5. Forecasting Fortune Teller\n\
