23. Crashing Wave\n\
\n\
Hmm, is Sold Out better than second Zuko's Conviction? Sold Out is removal—yes, we need removal. Keep Sold Out.\n\
\n\
Is Crashing Wave good? X waterbend cost, tap X creatures, distribute 3 stun counters. Stun counters keep them tapped longer. It's tempo removal. At {U}{U} plus waterbend X (tap your stuff). Decent. Keep over Lost Days? Lost Days is 5-mana permanent answer vs Crashing Wave tempo. The deck has only Deadly Precision and Sold Out as hard removal. Hmm, maybe I should include both Lost Days and cut... what? Maybe cut Pirate Peddlers or North Pole Patrol?\n\
\n\
The deck has a lot of 3-drops: Spirit Keeper x2, Peddlers, Hawks x2, Parrot, Patrol = 7 three-drops. Cut Patrol for Lost Days? Patrol's tap ability is relevant for board stalls. Peddlers with deathtouch + clue sac synergy. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Curve considerations: \n\
1-drops: Tiger-Seal, Callous Inspector (2)\n\
2-drops: Otter-Penguin, Knowledge Seeker, Fortune Teller, Waterbender Ascension (4)\n\
3-drops: Spirit Keeper x2, Peddlers, Hawk x2, Parrot, Patrol, Spirit Water Revival, Deadly Precision (10)\n\
4-drops: Hunters, Teo, Buzzard-Wasp, Waterbending Lesson, Sold Out (5)\n\
5+: Hama, Zuko's, Crashing Wave (3)\n\
\n\
That's a reasonable curve. Adding Lost Days (5) would make top heavy. I'll keep Crashing Wave as the flexible one and leave Lost Days out.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait—should I reconsider Buzzard-Wasp Colony? 4-mana 3/3? flier with sac outlet-ish (sac on ETB to draw) and counter theft. It's a flier for Teo, draws cards for the theme. Keep.\n\
\n\
Flexible Waterbender (4-mana 2/4 vigilance that becomes 5/2) is mediocre—cut. Canyon Crawler 6-mana—cut (though swampcycling helps fixing; but we have enough lands).\n\
\n\
Second Zuko's Conviction: I could include it over Crashing Wave for late-game grind. But Crashing Wave's board impact seems better for closing games. Keep one Zuko's.\n\
\n\
Final answer: 23 spells as listed.\n\
\n\
Analysis: UB \"draw two cards per turn\" deck with clue generation enabling payoffs; left out white cards (splash not worth it), Flexible Waterbender, Canyon Crawler, Lost Days, second Zuko's Conviction, Kyoshi Battle Fan.\n\
